Done. Spec produced at `artifacts/tmp102/outputs/spec_tmp102.md`.

**Pipeline summary:**
- Found esphome component `tmp102`; copied `tmp102.mdx` + source to `artifacts/tmp102/outputs/` and wrote `esphome_component.txt`
- Downloaded TI datasheet (1.1 MB) to `artifacts/tmp102/prompt0a/datasheet/tmp102.pdf`
- Converted to `tmp102_datasheet.md` (1104 lines) with pymupdf4llm
- Filled `template_chip.md` from the datasheet: I²C addressing (0x48–0x4B via ADD0), 6-pin SOT563 pinout, full register map (Temperature/Configuration/TLOW/THIGH), config bit fields, init sequence, and the `value = raw * 0.0625` conversion
- Feedback written to `feedback/tmp102/prompt0a.md`

Note: the esphome doc had no datasheet URL, so I used the TI product page directly (better than the 2013 wayback snapshot `analog.sh` returned).
